[
    {
        "text": "When you interact with an application, there are three fundamental ways for that application to transfer funds from the user. There's Transfer Approve and CPI Transfer with User Authorization. The first two are safe, but that CPI transfer with authorization can be dangerous, as the details of the transfer are not always visible. The CPI Guard token extension prohibits CPI calls without that user authorization, forcing programs to directly ask for that user's authority. This brings more transparency to wallets and other applications when they're asking users to transfer their money. Check out more on cpi guard on Solana.com.",
        "start": 320,
        "end": 40060,
        "confidence": 0.9799197,
        "channel": null,
        "speaker": "A",
